// Buff self-host port of `crates/buff-lang-buffhtml-parser/src/lib.rs` (P4.5).
//
// Buff `.buffhtml` Parser crate — 3-mode lexer + recursive-descent parser.
//
// Implements the T133 floor grammar (decision record
// `rsx-syntax-feasibility.md` §6 MUST-ship list):
//
// - HTML elements / tags / attributes
// - `{expr}` interpolation
// - `{#each}/{:else}/{/each}` loops
// - `{#if}/{:else if}/{:else}/{/if}` conditionals
// - Fragments `<> ... </>`
// - Child component composition (capitalized tags)
// - Default `<slot />`
// - Comments (`<!-- -->` HTML and `{# ... #}` Buff directive)
// - `<script lang="buff"> ... </script>` blocks
// - `on:event_modifier={handler}` event directives
// - Named props (`name: value`)
//
// Deferred per §6 (NOT implemented; emitted as a parse error with TODO):
// named slots, keyed each, spread props, two-way binding, await, `{@html}`.
//
// # Layout
//
// - `lexer`: byte-scanner producing a flat `BuffHtmlToken` stream.
//   The lexer has THREE modes per the decision record §3: `TEXT`,
//   `BUFF_CODE` (inside `{...}`), and `BUFF_DIRECTIVE` (inside `{#...}`,
//   `{:...}`, `{/...}`, `{@...}`).
// - `parser`: recursive-descent over the token stream -> `RsxTemplateFile`.
//
// Faithful 1:1 translation of the Rust reference. The Rust `lib.rs` is pure
// module wiring (`pub mod ...` + `pub use <mod>::...` re-exports). Buff has
// no `mod` keyword and no `pub use` glob — the M7 monolith loader (Phase 5)
// concatenates sibling `.buff` files in the same directory into a flat
// namespace, and `export` controls visibility per symbol. There is therefore
// nothing executable to translate here; this file is a documentation-only
// header that mirrors the Rust crate-doc comment block and records the
// translation decision.
//
// Translation decisions:
//   * `pub mod error; pub mod lexer; pub mod parser;` (Rust module
//     declarations) -> DELETED. Buff has no `mod` keyword; files in the same
//     directory are auto-linked once the M7 monolith loader is active. Until
//     then, single-file `buff check` treats cross-file references as opaque
//     forward references (per `self-host/ast/lib.buff` header lines 33-38).
//   * `pub use error::BuffHtmlParseError;` (re-export of a type) -> DELETED.
//     Buff has no syntax for cross-file re-export; callers `import
//     { BuffHtmlParseError } from "error"` directly once the monolith loader
//     lands.
//   * `pub use lexer::{tokenize, BuffHtmlToken, BuffHtmlTokenKind};`
//     (re-export of three symbols) -> DELETED for the same reason. Callers
//     reach these via `import { tokenize, BuffHtmlToken, BuffHtmlTokenKind }
//     from "lexer"`.
//   * `pub use parser::parse;` -> DELETED. Callers `import { parse }
//     from "parser"`.
//
// The three sibling files in this directory (`error.buff`, `lexer.buff`,
// `parser.buff`) each define their own local `Span` / `SourceId` stand-ins
// so they pass single-file `buff check` today; the M7 monolith loader will
// deduplicate them when it lands.